#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198154 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b31f2bdc-c267-5fc7-bd0f-283777ee4fee" :knowledge-point/title "The Derivative of a Three-Component Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/id #uuid "a5637d71-22d4-548e-ad36-d09bff61d643" :question/math-academy-id "e-2398" :question/problem "Find the derivative of  $\\mathbf f(t) = \\langle \\sin t ,\\cos t , t \\rangle$ at $t= \\dfrac{\\pi}4.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find $\\mathbf f'(t)$ by differentiating each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute $\\mathbf f'\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}4\\right),$ we substitute $t=\\dfrac{\\pi}4$ into the expression for $\\mathbf f'(t)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}),\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}),\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\,-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198157 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "072ad553-dd0b-58e0-b3e2-082c6d9866dd" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Derivative of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/id #uuid "c737d317-8e09-5ccb-b816-b5f56e925ba9" :question/math-academy-id "e-609" :question/problem "Given that $\\mathbf r(t) = \\langle 10t^4 ,\\, 6\\ln t\\rangle,$ what is $\\mathbf r'\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)?$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t) = 10t^4,$ we have\n\n$$\nx'(t) = 40t^3,\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\nx'\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right) = 40\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)^3 = 5.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t) = 6 \\ln t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t)=\\frac{6}{t},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\ny'\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right) = \\dfrac{6}{\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)}=12.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(\\frac{1}{2}) & =⟨{x}^{′}(\\frac{1}{2}),\\,{y}^{′}(\\frac{1}{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5,\\,12⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198158 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f0e2596-73d6-540c-af84-b19a943da6a8" :knowledge-point/title "The Second Derivative of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/id #uuid "cde8f304-4937-5eb7-a8e1-a08355ee4d4e" :question/math-academy-id "e-611" :question/problem "Given that $\\mathbf r(t) = \\langle t^6,\\, t^5\\rangle,$ Calculate $\\mathbf r''(t).$" :question/worked-solution "To find the second derivative of a vector-valued function, we find the second derivatives of the components.\n\n- For $x(t) = t^6,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & =6{t}^{5} \\\\ {x}^{″}(t) & =30{t}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $y(t) = t^5,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =5{t}^{4} \\\\ {y}^{″}(t) & =20{t}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨{x}^{″}(t),\\,{y}^{″}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨30{t}^{4},\\,20{t}^{3}⟩ \\\\  & =10⟨3{t}^{4},\\,2{t}^{3}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198870 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b31f2bdc-c267-5fc7-bd0f-283777ee4fee" :knowledge-point/title "The Derivative of a Three-Component Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8137a8ff-b68c-5072-bf40-cff9ad06083f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3t^{2} + 10t \\\\ \\sec^{2} t \\\\ 6^{t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197456} {:answer/id #uuid "95f6c6ca-8b95-5860-8bee-4d06fdc902ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3t^{2} + 10t \\\\ \\sec^{2} t \\\\ 6^{t}\\ln 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197457} {:answer/id #uuid "edb3be8b-3a96-5052-a676-0fd51e412c9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}t^{2} + 5t \\\\ \\sec^{2} t \\\\ 6^{t}\\ln 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197458} {:answer/id #uuid "43fe1132-8933-5074-b351-2af945d72ab4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3t^{2} + 10t \\\\ \\sec t \\\\ 6^{t}\\ln 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197459} {:answer/id #uuid "7b49052a-5bf2-5992-9e86-a07a5e369039" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3t^{2} + 10t \\\\ \\csc^{2} t \\\\ 6^{t}\\ln 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197460}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "95f6c6ca-8b95-5860-8bee-4d06fdc902ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3t^{2} + 10t \\\\ \\sec^{2} t \\\\ 6^{t}\\ln 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197457} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c9ec6a6-0db9-5452-8f08-393cefaecc44" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197455}] :question/id #uuid "74e54a04-5388-5c59-b810-bdb93752e4b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-32415" :question/problem "Calculate $f^{′}(t)$ given that $f(t) = \\begin{bmatrix}t^{3} + 5t^{2} \\\\ \\tan t \\\\ 6^{t}\\end{bmatrix}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186296337 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "072ad553-dd0b-58e0-b3e2-082c6d9866dd" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Derivative of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5aff8bf9-2be5-5fea-9bca-d1ab4e8518e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,8{e}^{t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296339} {:answer/id #uuid "a02992c9-bb0d-53e8-8eee-9ab879a36726" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,8{e}^{t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296340} {:answer/id #uuid "5af4e518-15cd-5056-b76e-8979a49a9066" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,{e}^{t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296341} {:answer/id #uuid "499b53ad-0f19-573e-9e6f-6c6b1e5c759d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{2}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296342} {:answer/id #uuid "7d81d374-3be8-5dad-bad8-7bbfcbcd0fd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296343}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5aff8bf9-2be5-5fea-9bca-d1ab4e8518e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,8{e}^{t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296339} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe23e1b9-a6e4-5d5c-acb8-5f1d8899b18b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296338}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6eef8652-af24-51e5-8f51-46e17a486c11" :question/math-academy-id "q-50373" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}-1),\\,8{e}^{t}⟩,$ ${r}^{′}(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}-1),$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}-1}.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)=8{e}^{t},$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=8{e}^{t}.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨{x}^{′}(t),\\,{y}^{′}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,8{e}^{t}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
